    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "28ac7555_5ebeec6e",
        "filename": "microdroid/init.rc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 54,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-06-01T11:22:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The reason why this needs to run before apexd is that the list of APEXes are right now coming from untrusted source (i.e. the metadata partition). The list should be from the payload config. The medata partition should provide only the mapping of the (name, partition) pairs, but not the list of APEXes that need to be activated in this VM.",
      "parentUuid": "963d81a5_8169cd78",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 54,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 54,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "8fdcb00c9e2118f52832efff0a605da15fec82b8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b788715e_9e6a2f4d",
        "filename": "microdroid/init.rc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 54,
      "author": {
        "id": 1415877
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-06-01T11:44:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "But isn\u0027t the path for the VM payload config retrieved from the metadata partition?\n\nBtw, if we want apexd to activate what it is said so, we could do that by passing the list of apexes to apexd with arguments(e.g. apexd --vm --apexes\u003d/dev/block/by-name/apex1:/dev/block/by-name/apex2:/dev/block/by-name/apex3...). To do that, apexd should be started by microdroid_manager as well.\n\nzipfuse might need to be \"bootstrap\" (in Android.bp) so that it can be started before apexd.\n\n* microdroid_manager reads metadata partition\n* microdroid_manager starts zipfuse: zipfuse \u003capk partition\u003e /mnt/apk\n* micordroid_manager starts apexd: apexd --vm \u003clist of apex partitions\u003e\n* (init should wait for \"apexd.status\u003dready\" to start other services)\n* ...",
      "parentUuid": "28ac7555_5ebeec6e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 54,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 54,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "8fdcb00c9e2118f52832efff0a605da15fec82b8",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0eadb865_934ba8b7",
        "filename": "microdroid/init.rc",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 54,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-06-01T12:26:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We could let microdroid_manager to start apexd. But the list of apexes can be passed via other means: sysprop, a file in tmpfs, etc. We can even let apexd parse the payload config by itself by providing a library doing that. The main role of microdroid_manager is to stop booting when the list of APEXes it read from the config is different from the list of APEXes it retrieved from the identity disk.\n\n\u003e zipfuse might need to be \"bootstrap\" (in Android.bp) so that it can be started before apexd.\n\nThat\u0027s correct. Or we could run apexd twice: once before microdroid_manager to activate the critical APEXes like the runtime and once again after microdroid_manager to activate the user-specified APEXes on top of the runtime APEX.",
      "parentUuid": "b788715e_9e6a2f4d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 54,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 54,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "8fdcb00c9e2118f52832efff0a605da15fec82b8",
